#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:2
msgid "1.5.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:4
msgid ""
"Q.any now annotates its error message to clarify that Q.any was involved "
"and includes only the last error emitted. (Ivan Etchart)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:6
msgid ""
"Avoid domain.dispose during tests in preparation for Node.js 9. (Anna "
"Henningsen)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:9
msgid "1.5.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:11
msgid "Q.any gives an error message from the last rejected promise"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:12
msgid "Throw if callback supplied to \"finally\" is invalid (@grahamrhay)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:13
msgid ""
"Long stack trace improvements, can now construct long stack traces across"
" rethrows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:16
msgid "1.4.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:18
msgid ""
"Address an issue that prevented Q from being used as a `<script>` for "
"Firefox add-ons. Q can now be used in any environment that provides "
"`window` or `self` globals, favoring `window` since add-ons have an an "
"immutable `self` that is distinct from `window`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:23
msgid "1.4.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:25
msgid "Add `noConflict` support for use in `<script>` (@jahnjw)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:27
msgid "1.3.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:29
msgid ""
"Add tracking for unhandled and handled rejections in Node.js "
"(@benjamingr)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:31
msgid "1.2.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:33
msgid "Fix Node.js environment detection for modern Browserify (@kahnjw)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:35
msgid "1.2.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:37
msgid ""
"Added Q.any(promisesArray) method (@vergara). Returns a promise fulfilled"
" with the value of the first resolved promise in promisesArray. If all "
"promises in promisesArray are rejected, it returns a rejected promise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:42
msgid "1.1.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:44
msgid ""
"Removed extraneous files from the npm package by using the \"files\" "
"whitelist in package.json instead of the .npmignore blacklist. (@anton-"
"rudeshko)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:48
msgid "1.1.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:50
msgid ""
"Fix a pair of regressions in bootstrapping, one which precluded WebWorker"
" support, and another that precluded support in ``<script>`` usage "
"outright. #607"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:54
msgid "1.1.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:56
msgid ""
"Adds support for enabling long stack traces in node.js by setting "
"environment variable `Q_DEBUG=1`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:58
msgid ""
"Introduces the `tap` method to promises, which will see a value pass "
"through without alteration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:60
msgid "Use instanceof to recognize own promise instances as opposed to thenables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:62
msgid "Construct timeout errors with `code === ETIMEDOUT` (Kornel Lesiński)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:63
msgid "More descriminant CommonJS module environment detection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:64
msgid ""
"Dropped continuous integration for Node.js 0.6 and 0.8 because of changes"
" to npm that preclude the use of new `^` version predicate operator in "
"any transitive dependency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:67
msgid "Users can now override `Q.nextTick`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:69
msgid "1.0.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:71
msgid ""
"Adds support for `Q.Promise`, which implements common usage of the ES6 "
"`Promise` constructor and its methods. `Promise` does not have a valid "
"promise constructor and a proper implementation awaits version 2 of Q."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:75
msgid ""
"Removes the console stopgap for a promise inspector. This no longer works"
" with any degree of reliability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:77
msgid ""
"Fixes support for content security policies that forbid eval. Now using "
"the `StopIteration` global to distinguish SpiderMonkey generators from "
"ES6 generators, assuming that they will never coexist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:82
msgid "1.0.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:84
msgid ""
":cake: This is all but a re-release of version 0.9, which has settled "
"into a gentle maintenance mode and rightly deserves an official 1.0. An "
"ambitious 2.0 release is already around the corner, but 0.9/1.0 have been"
" distributed far and wide and demand long term support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:89
msgid ""
"Q will now attempt to post a debug message in browsers regardless of "
"whether window.Touch is defined. Chrome at least now has this property "
"regardless of whether touch is supported by the underlying hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:93
msgid ""
"Remove deprecation warning from `promise.valueOf`. The function is called"
" by the browser in various ways so there is no way to distinguish usage "
"that should be migrated from usage that cannot be altered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:98
msgid "0.9.7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:100
msgid ""
":warning: `q.min.js` is no longer checked-in.  It is however still "
"created by Grunt and NPM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:102
msgid ""
"Fixes a bug that inhibited `Q.async` with implementations of the new ES6 "
"generators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:104
msgid ""
"Fixes a bug with `nextTick` affecting Safari 6.0.5 the first time a page "
"loads when an `iframe` is involved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:106
msgid "Introduces `passByCopy`, `join`, and `race`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:107
msgid ""
"Shows stack traces or error messages on the console, instead of `Error` "
"objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:109
msgid "Elimintates wrapper methods for improved performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:110
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`Q.all` now propagates progress notifications of the form you might "
"expect of ES6 iterations, `{value, index}` where the `value` is the "
"progress notification from the promise at `index`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:114
msgid "0.9.6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:116
msgid ""
"Fixes a bug in recognizing the difference between compatible Q promises, "
"and Q promises from before the implementation of \"inspect\". The latter "
"are now coerced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:119
msgid ""
"Fixes an infinite asynchronous coercion cycle introduced by former "
"solution, in two independently sufficient ways.  1.) All promises "
"returned by makePromise now implement \"inspect\", albeit a default that "
"reports that the promise has an \"unknown\" state.  2.) The "
"implementation of \"then/when\" is now in \"then\" instead of \"when\", "
"so that the responsibility to \"coerce\" the given promise rests solely "
"in the \"when\" method and the \"then\" method may assume that \"this\" "
"is a promise of the right type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:127
msgid ""
"Refactors `nextTick` to use an unrolled microtask within Q regardless of "
"how new ticks a requested. #316 @rkatic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:130
msgid "0.9.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:132
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Introduces `inspect` for getting the state of a promise as `{state: "
"\"fulfilled\" | \"rejected\" | \"pending\", value | reason}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:134
msgid ""
"Introduces `allSettled` which produces an array of promises states for "
"the input promises once they have all \"settled\".  This is in accordance"
" with a discussion on Promises/A+ that \"settled\" refers to a promise "
"that is \"fulfilled\" or \"rejected\".  \"resolved\" refers to a deferred"
" promise that has been \"resolved\" to another promise, \"sealing its "
"fate\" to the fate of the successor promise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:140
msgid ""
"Long stack traces are now off by default.  Set `Q.longStackSupport` to "
"true to enable long stack traces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:142
msgid ""
"Long stack traces can now follow the entire asynchronous history of a "
"promise, not just a single jump."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:144
msgid ""
"Introduces `spawn` for an immediately invoked asychronous generator. "
"@jlongster"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:146
msgid ""
"Support for *experimental* synonyms `mapply`, `mcall`, `nmapply`, "
"`nmcall` for method invocation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:149
msgid "0.9.4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:151
msgid ""
"`isPromise` and `isPromiseAlike` now always returns a boolean (even for "
"falsy values). #284 @lfac-pt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:153
msgid "Support for ES6 Generators in `async` #288 @andywingo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:154
msgid "Clear duplicate promise rejections from dispatch methods #238 @SLaks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:155
msgid ""
"Unhandled rejection API #296 @domenic `stopUnhandledRejectionTracking`, "
"`getUnhandledReasons`, `resetUnhandledRejections`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:159
msgid "0.9.3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:161
msgid ""
"Add the ability to give `Q.timeout`'s errors a custom error message. #270"
" @jgrenon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:163
msgid ""
"Fix Q's call-stack busting behavior in Node.js 0.10, by switching from "
"`process.nextTick` to `setImmediate`. #254 #259"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:165
msgid ""
"Fix Q's behavior when used with the Mocha test runner in the browser, "
"since Mocha introduces a fake `process` global without a `nextTick` "
"property. #267"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:167
msgid ""
"Fix some, but not all, cases wherein Q would give false positives in its "
"unhandled rejection detection (#252). A fix for other cases (#238) is "
"hopefully coming soon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:170
msgid "Made `Q.promise` throw early if given a non-function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:172
msgid "0.9.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:174
msgid "Pass through progress notifications when using `timeout`. #229 @omares"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:175
msgid "Pass through progress notifications when using `delay`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:176
msgid "Fix `nbind` to actually bind the `thisArg`. #232 @davidpadbury"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:178
msgid "0.9.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:180
msgid ""
"Made the AMD detection compatible with the RequireJS optimizer's "
"`namespace` option. #225 @terinjokes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:182
msgid ""
"Fix side effects from `valueOf`, and thus from `isFulfilled`, "
"`isRejected`, and `isPending`. #226 @benjamn"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:185
msgid "0.9.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:187
msgid ""
"This release removes many layers of deprecated methods and brings Q "
"closer to alignment with Mark Miller’s TC39 [strawman][] for concurrency."
" At the same time, it fixes many bugs and adds a few features around "
"error handling. Finally, it comes with an updated and comprehensive [API "
"Reference][]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:195
msgid "API Cleanup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:197
msgid ""
"The following deprecated or undocumented methods have been removed. Their"
" replacements are listed here:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:260
msgid ""
"(*) Use of ``thisp`` is discouraged. For calling methods, use ``post`` or"
" ``invoke``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:263
msgid "Alignment with the Concurrency Strawman"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:265
msgid ""
"Q now exports a `Q(value)` function, an alias for `resolve`. `Q.call`, "
"`Q.apply`, and `Q.bind` were removed to make room for the same methods on"
" the function prototype."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:268
msgid "`invoke` has been aliased to `send` in all its forms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:269
msgid "`post` with no method name acts like `fapply`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:271
msgid "Error Handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:273
msgid ""
"Long stack traces can be turned off by setting `Q.stackJumpLimit` to "
"zero. In the future, this property will be used to fine tune how many "
"stack jumps are retained in long stack traces; for now, anything nonzero "
"is treated as one (since Q only tracks one stack jump at the moment, see "
"#144). #168"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:277
msgid ""
"In Node.js, if there are unhandled rejections when the process exits, "
"they are output to the console. #115"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:280
msgid "Other"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:282
msgid "`delete` and `set` (née `put`) no longer have a fulfillment value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:283
msgid ""
"Q promises are no longer frozen, which [helps with "
"performance](http://code.google.com/p/v8/issues/detail?id=1858)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:285
msgid "`thenReject` is now included, as a counterpart to `thenResolve`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:286
msgid "The included browser `nextTick` shim is now faster. #195 @rkatic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:288
msgid "Bug Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:290
msgid "Q now works in Internet Explorer 10. #186 @ForbesLindesay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:291
msgid ""
"`fbind` no longer hard-binds the returned function's `this` to "
"`undefined`. #202"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:293
msgid "`Q.reject` no longer leaks memory. #148"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:294
msgid "`npost` with no arguments now works. #207"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:295
msgid "`allResolved` now works with non-Q promises (\"thenables\"). #179"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:296
msgid ""
"`keys` behavior is now correct even in browsers without native "
"`Object.keys`. #192 @rkatic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:298
msgid ""
"`isRejected` and the `exception` property now work correctly if the "
"rejection reason is falsy. #198"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:301
msgid "Internals and Advanced"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:303
msgid ""
"The internal interface for a promise now uses `dispatchPromise(resolve, "
"op, operands)` instead of `sendPromise(op, resolve, ...operands)`, which "
"reduces the cases where Q needs to do argument slicing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:307
msgid ""
"The internal protocol uses different operands. \"put\" is now \"set\". "
"\"del\" is now \"delete\". \"view\" and \"viewInfo\" have been removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:309
msgid ""
"`Q.fulfill` has been added. It is distinct from `Q.resolve` in that it "
"does not pass promises through, nor coerces promises from other systems. "
"The promise becomes the fulfillment value. This is only recommended for "
"use when trying to fulfill a promise with an object that has a `then` "
"function that is at the same time not a promise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:315
msgid "0.8.12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:316
msgid ""
"Treat foreign promises as unresolved in `Q.isFulfilled`; this lets "
"`Q.all` work on arrays containing foreign promises. #154"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:318
msgid ""
"Fix minor incompliances with the [Promises/A+ spec][] and [test suite][]."
" #157 #158"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:324
msgid "0.8.11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:326
msgid ""
"Added ``nfcall``, ``nfapply``, and ``nfbind`` as ``thisp``-less versions "
"of ``ncall``, ``napply``, and ``nbind``. The latter are now deprecated. "
"#142"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:328
msgid ""
"Long stack traces no longer cause linearly-growing memory usage when "
"chaining promises together. #111"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:330
msgid ""
"Inspecting ``error.stack`` in a rejection handler will now give a long "
"stack trace. #103"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:332
msgid ""
"Fixed ``Q.timeout`` to clear its timeout handle when the promise is "
"rejected; previously, it kept the event loop alive until the timeout "
"period expired. #145 @dfilatov"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:335
msgid ""
"Added `q/queue` module, which exports an infinite promise queue "
"constructor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:338
msgid "0.8.10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:340
msgid ""
"Added ``done`` as a replacement for ``end``, taking the usual "
"fulfillment, rejection, and progress handlers. It's essentially "
"equivalent to ``then(f, r, p).end()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:343
msgid ""
"Added ``Q.onerror``, a settable error trap that you can use to get full "
"stack traces for uncaught errors. #94"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:345
msgid ""
"Added ``thenResolve`` as a shortcut for returning a constant value once a"
" promise is fulfilled. #108 @ForbesLindesay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:347
msgid ""
"Various tweaks to progress notification, including propagation and "
"transformation of progress values and only forwarding a single progress "
"object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:350
msgid ""
"Renamed ``nend`` to ``nodeify``. It no longer returns an always-fulfilled"
" promise when a Node callback is passed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:352
msgid ""
"``deferred.resolve`` and ``deferred.reject`` no longer (sometimes) return"
" ``deferred.promise``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:354
msgid ""
"Fixed stack traces getting mangled if they hit ``end`` twice. #116 #121 "
"@ef4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:355
msgid ""
"Fixed ``ninvoke`` and ``npost`` to work on promises for objects with Node"
" methods. #134"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:357
msgid ""
"Fixed accidental coercion of objects with nontrivial ``valueOf`` methods,"
" like ``Date``s, by the promise's ``valueOf`` method. #135"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:359
msgid ""
"Fixed ``spread`` not calling the passed rejection handler if given a "
"rejected promise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:362
msgid "0.8.9"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:364
msgid "Added ``nend``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:365
msgid ""
"Added preliminary progress notification support, via "
"``promise.then(onFulfilled, onRejected, onProgress)``, "
"``promise.progress(onProgress)``, and "
"``deferred.notify(...progressData)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:368
msgid ""
"Made ``put`` and ``del`` return the object acted upon for easier "
"chaining. #84"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:370
msgid "Fixed coercion cycles with cooperating promises. #106"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:372
msgid "0.8.7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:374
msgid "Support [Montage Require](http://github.com/kriskowal/mr)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:376
msgid "0.8.6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:378
msgid "Fixed ``npost`` and ``ninvoke`` to pass the correct ``thisp``. #74"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:379
msgid "Fixed various cases involving unorthodox rejection reasons. #73 #90 @ef4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:381
msgid "Fixed double-resolving of misbehaved custom promises. #75"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:382
msgid ""
"Sped up ``Q.all`` for arrays contain already-resolved promises or scalar "
"values. @ForbesLindesay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:384
msgid "Made stack trace filtering work when concatenating assets. #93 @ef4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:385
msgid "Added warnings for deprecated methods. @ForbesLindesay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:386
msgid ""
"Added ``.npmignore`` file so that dependent packages get a slimmer "
"``node_modules`` directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:389
msgid "0.8.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:391
msgid "Added preliminary support for long traces (@domenic)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:392
msgid ""
"Added ``fapply``, ``fcall``, ``fbind`` for non-thisp promised function "
"calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:394
msgid "Added ``return`` for async generators, where generators are implemented."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:396
msgid ""
"Rejected promises now have an \"exception\" property.  If an object "
"isRejected(object), then object.valueOf().exception will be the wrapped "
"error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:399
msgid "Added Jasmine specifications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:400
msgid "Support Internet Explorers 7–9 (with multiple bug fixes @domenic)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:401
msgid "Support Firefox 12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:402
msgid "Support Safari 5.1.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:403
msgid "Support Chrome 18"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:405
msgid "0.8.4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:407
msgid ""
"WARNING: ``promise.timeout`` is now rejected with an ``Error`` object and"
" the message now includes the duration of the timeout in miliseconds.  "
"This doesn't constitute (in my opinion) a backward-incompatibility since "
"it is a change of an undocumented and unspecified public behavior, but if"
" you happened to depend on the exception being a string, you will need to"
" revise your code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:413
msgid ""
"Added ``deferred.makeNodeResolver()`` to replace the more cryptic "
"``deferred.node()`` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:415
msgid ""
"Added experimental ``Q.promise(maker(resolve, reject))`` to make a "
"promise inside a callback, such that thrown exceptions in the callback "
"are converted and the resolver and rejecter are arguments. This is a "
"shorthand for making a deferred directly and inspired by @gozala’s stream"
" constructor pattern and the Microsoft Windows Metro Promise constructor "
"interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:421
msgid ""
"Added experimental ``Q.begin()`` that is intended to kick off chains of "
"``.then`` so that each of these can be reordered without having to edit "
"the new and former first step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:425
msgid "0.8.3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:427
msgid ""
"Added ``isFulfilled``, ``isRejected``, and ``isResolved`` to the promise "
"prototype."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:429
msgid ""
"Added ``allResolved`` for waiting for every promise to either be "
"fulfilled or rejected, without propagating an error. @utvara #53"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:431
msgid ""
"Added ``Q.bind`` as a method to transform functions that return and throw"
" into promise-returning functions. See [an "
"example](https://gist.github.com/1782808). @domenic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:434
msgid ""
"Renamed ``node`` export to ``nbind``, and added ``napply`` to complete "
"the set. ``node`` remains as deprecated. @domenic #58"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:436
msgid ""
"Renamed ``Method`` export to ``sender``.  ``Method`` remains as "
"deprecated and will be removed in the next major version since I expect "
"it has very little usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:439
msgid "Added browser console message indicating a live list of unhandled errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:441
msgid ""
"Added support for ``msSetImmediate`` (IE10) or ``setImmediate`` "
"(available via [polyfill](https://github.com/NobleJS/setImmediate)) as a "
"browser-side ``nextTick`` implementation. #44 #50 #59"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:444
msgid ""
"Stopped using the event-queue dependency, which was in place for Narwhal "
"support: now directly using ``process.nextTick``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:446
msgid ""
"WARNING: EXPERIMENTAL: added ``finally`` alias for ``fin``, ``catch`` "
"alias for ``fail``, ``try`` alias for ``call``, and ``delete`` alias for "
"``del``.  These properties are enquoted in the library for cross-browser "
"compatibility, but may be used as property names in modern engines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:452
msgid "0.8.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:454
msgid "Deprecated ``ref`` in favor of ``resolve`` as recommended by @domenic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:456
msgid "Update event-queue dependency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:458
msgid "0.8.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:460
msgid "Fixed Opera bug. #35 @cadorn"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:461
msgid "Fixed ``Q.all([])`` #32 @domenic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:463
msgid "0.8.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:465
msgid ""
"WARNING: ``enqueue`` removed.  Use ``nextTick`` instead. This is more "
"consistent with NodeJS and (subjectively) more explicit and intuitive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:468
msgid ""
"WARNING: ``def`` removed.  Use ``master`` instead.  The term ``def`` was "
"too confusing to new users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:470
msgid "WARNING: ``spy`` removed in favor of ``fin``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:471
msgid "WARNING: ``wait`` removed. Do ``all(args).get(0)`` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:472
msgid "WARNING: ``join`` removed. Do ``all(args).spread(callback)`` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:473
msgid ""
"WARNING: Removed the ``Q`` function module.exports alias for ``Q.ref``. "
"It conflicts with ``Q.apply`` in weird ways, making it uncallable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:476
msgid ""
"Revised ``delay`` so that it accepts both ``(value, timeout)`` and "
"``(timeout)`` variations based on arguments length."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:479
msgid ""
"Added ``ref().spread(cb(...args))``, a variant of ``then`` that spreads "
"an array across multiple arguments. Useful with ``all()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:482
msgid ""
"Added ``defer().node()`` Node callback generator.  The callback accepts "
"``(error, value)`` or ``(error, ...values)``.  For multiple value "
"arguments, the fulfillment value is an array, useful in conjunction with "
"``spread``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:487
msgid ""
"Added ``node`` and ``ncall``, both with the signature ``(fun, thisp_opt, "
"...args)``.  The former is a decorator and the latter calls immediately."
"  ``node`` optional binds and partially applies.  ``ncall`` can bind and "
"pass arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:493
msgid "0.7.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:495
msgid "Fixed thenable promise assimilation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:497
msgid "0.7.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:499
msgid ""
"Stopped shimming ``Array.prototype.reduce``. The enumerable property has "
"bad side-effects.  Libraries that depend on this (for example, QQ) will "
"need to be revised."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:503
msgid "0.7.0 - BACKWARD INCOMPATIBILITY"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:505
msgid "WARNING: Removed ``report`` and ``asap``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:506
msgid ""
"WARNING: The ``callback`` argument of the ``fin`` function no longer "
"receives any arguments. Thus, it can be used to call functions that "
"should not receive arguments on resolution.  Use ``when``, ``then``, or "
"``fail`` if you need a value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:511
msgid "IMPORTANT: Fixed a bug in the use of ``MessageChannel`` for ``nextTick``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:513
msgid "Renamed ``enqueue`` to ``nextTick``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:514
msgid ""
"Added experimental ``view`` and ``viewInfo`` for creating views of "
"promises either when or before they're fulfilled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:517
msgid ""
"Shims are now externally applied so subsequent scripts or dependees can "
"use them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:519
msgid "Improved minification results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:520
msgid "Improved readability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:522
msgid "0.6.0 - BACKWARD INCOMPATIBILITY"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:524
msgid ""
"WARNING: In practice, the implementation of ``spy`` and the name ``fin`` "
"were useful.  I've removed the old ``fin`` implementation and "
"renamed/aliased ``spy``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:527
msgid ""
"The \"q\" module now exports its ``ref`` function as a \"Q\" constructor,"
" with module systems that support exports assignment including NodeJS, "
"RequireJS, and when used as a ``<script>`` tag. Notably, strictly "
"compliant CommonJS does not support this, but UncommonJS does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:532
msgid ""
"Added ``async`` decorator for generators that use yield to \"trampoline\""
" promises. In engines that support generators (SpiderMonkey), this will "
"greatly reduce the need for nested callbacks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:536
msgid "Made ``when`` chainable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:537
msgid "Made ``all`` chainable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:539
msgid "0.5.3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:541
msgid ""
"Added ``all`` and refactored ``join`` and ``wait`` to use it.  All of "
"these will now reject at the earliest rejection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:545
msgid "0.5.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:547
msgid ""
"Minor improvement to ``spy``; now waits for resolution of callback "
"promise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:550
msgid "0.5.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:552
msgid ""
"Made most Q API methods chainable on promise objects, and turned the "
"previous promise-methods of ``join``, ``wait``, and ``report`` into Q API"
" methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:555
msgid ""
"Added ``apply`` and ``call`` to the Q API, and ``apply`` as a promise "
"handler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:557
msgid ""
"Added ``fail``, ``fin``, and ``spy`` to Q and the promise prototype for "
"convenience when observing rejection, fulfillment and rejection, or just "
"observing without affecting the resolution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:561
msgid ""
"Renamed ``def`` (although ``def`` remains shimmed until the next major "
"release) to ``master``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:563
msgid ""
"Switched to using ``MessageChannel`` for next tick task enqueue in "
"browsers that support it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:566
msgid "0.5.0 - MINOR BACKWARD INCOMPATIBILITY"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:568
msgid "Exceptions are no longer reported when consumed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:569
msgid ""
"Removed ``error`` from the API.  Since exceptions are getting consumed, "
"throwing them in an errback causes the exception to silently disappear.  "
"Use ``end``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:572
msgid ""
"Added ``end`` as both an API method and a promise-chain ending method.  "
"It causes propagated rejections to be thrown, which allows Node to write "
"stack traces and emit ``uncaughtException`` events, and browsers to "
"likewise emit ``onerror`` and log to the console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:577
msgid ""
"Added ``join`` and ``wait`` as promise chain functions, so you can wait "
"for variadic promises, returning your own promise back, or join variadic "
"promises, resolving with a callback that receives variadic fulfillment "
"values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:582
msgid "0.4.4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:584
msgid "``end`` no longer returns a promise. It is the end of the promise chain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:586
msgid ""
"Stopped reporting thrown exceptions in ``when`` callbacks and errbacks.  "
"These must be explicitly reported through ``.end()``, ``.then(null, "
"Q.error)``, or some other mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:590
msgid ""
"Added ``report`` as an API method, which can be used as an errback to "
"report and propagate an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:592
msgid ""
"Added ``report`` as a promise-chain method, so an error can be reported "
"if it passes such a gate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:595
msgid "0.4.3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:597
msgid ""
"Fixed ``<script>`` support that regressed with 0.4.2 because of \"use "
"strict\" in the module system multi-plexer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:601
msgid "0.4.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:603
msgid "Added support for RequireJS (jburke)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:605
msgid "0.4.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:607
msgid ""
"Added an \"end\" method to the promise prototype, as a shorthand for "
"waiting for the promise to be resolved gracefully, and failing to do so, "
"to dump an error message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:612
msgid "0.4.0 - BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:614
msgid ""
"*Removed the utility modules. NPM and Node no longer expose any module "
"except the main module.  These have been moved and merged into the \"qq\""
" package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:617
msgid ""
"*In a non-CommonJS browser, q.js can be used as a script. It now creates "
"a Q global variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:619
msgid "Fixed thenable assimilation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:620
msgid ""
"Fixed some issues with asap, when it resolves to undefined, or throws an "
"exception."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:623
msgid "0.3.0 - BACKWARD-INCOMPATIBLE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:625
msgid ""
"The `post` method has been reverted to its original signature, as "
"provided in Tyler Close's `ref_send` API. That is, `post` accepts two "
"arguments, the second of which is an arbitrary object, but usually "
"invocation arguments as an `Array`.  To provide variadic arguments to "
"`post`, there is a new `invoke` function that posts the variadic "
"arguments to the value given in the first argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:633
msgid ""
"The `defined` method has been moved from `q` to `q/util` since it gets no"
" use in practice but is still theoretically useful."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:636
msgid ""
"The `Promise` constructor has been renamed to `makePromise` to be "
"consistent with the convention that functions that do not require the "
"`new` keyword to be used as constructors have camelCase names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:640
msgid ""
"The `isResolved` function has been renamed to `isFulfilled`.  There is a "
"new `isResolved` function that indicates whether a value is not a promise"
" or, if it is a promise, whether it has been either fulfilled or "
"rejected.  The code has been revised to reflect this nuance in "
"terminology."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:647
msgid "0.2.10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:649
msgid "Added `join` to `\"q/util\"` for variadically joining multiple promises."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:652
msgid "0.2.9"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:654
msgid ""
"The future-compatible `invoke` method has been added, to replace `post`, "
"since `post` will become backward- incompatible in the next major "
"release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:657
msgid ""
"Exceptions thrown in the callbacks of a `when` call are now emitted to "
"Node's `\"uncaughtException\"` `process` event in addition to being "
"returned as a rejection reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:661
msgid "0.2.8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:663
msgid ""
"Exceptions thrown in the callbacks of a `when` call are now consumed, "
"warned, and transformed into rejections of the promise returned by "
"`when`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:667
msgid "0.2.7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:669
msgid ""
"Fixed a minor bug in thenable assimilation, regressed because of the "
"change in the forwarding protocol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:671
msgid ""
"Fixed behavior of \"q/util\" `deep` method on dates and other primitives."
" Github issue #11."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:674
msgid "0.2.6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:676
msgid ""
"Thenables (objects with a \"then\" method) are accepted and provided, "
"bringing this implementation of Q into conformance with Promises/A, B, "
"and D."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:679
msgid "Added `makePromise`, to replace the `Promise` function eventually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:681
msgid ""
"Rejections are now also duck-typed. A rejection is a promise with a "
"valueOf method that returns a rejection descriptor. A rejection "
"descriptor has a \"promiseRejected\" property equal to \"true\" and a "
"\"reason\" property corresponding to the rejection reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:686
msgid ""
"Altered the `makePromise` API such that the `fallback` method no longer "
"receives a superfluous `resolved` method after the `operator`.  The "
"fallback method is responsible only for returning a resolution.  This "
"breaks an undocumented API, so third-party API's depending on the "
"previous undocumented behavior may break."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:693
msgid "0.2.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:695
msgid ""
"Changed promises into a duck-type such that multiple instances of the Q "
"module can exchange promise objects. A promise is now defined as \"an "
"object that implements the `promiseSend(op, resolved, ...)` method and "
"`valueOf`\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:699
msgid "Exceptions in promises are now captured and returned as rejections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:702
msgid "0.2.4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:704
msgid ""
"Fixed bug in `ref` that prevented `del` messages from being received "
"(gozala)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:706
msgid "Fixed a conflict with FireFox 4; constructor property is now read-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:709
msgid "0.2.3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:711
msgid "Added `keys` message to promises and to the promise API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:713
msgid "0.2.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:715
msgid "Added boilerplate to `q/queue` and `q/util`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:716
msgid "Fixed missing dependency to `q/queue`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:718
msgid "0.2.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:720
msgid ""
"The `resolve` and `reject` methods of `defer` objects now return the "
"resolution promise for convenience."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:722
msgid ""
"Added `q/util`, which provides `step`, `delay`, `shallow`, `deep`, and "
"three reduction orders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:724
msgid "Added `q/queue` module for a promise `Queue`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:725
msgid "Added `q-comm` to the list of compatible libraries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:726
msgid "Deprecated `defined` from `q`, with intent to move it to `q/util`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:729
msgid "0.2.0 - BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:731
msgid ""
"Changed post(ref, name, args) to variadic post(ref, name, ...args). "
"BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:733
msgid ""
"Added a def(value) method to annotate an object as being necessarily a "
"local value that cannot be serialized, such that inter-process/worker/vat"
" promise communication libraries will send messages to it, but never send"
" it back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:738
msgid ""
"Added a send(value, op, ...args) method to the public API, for forwarding"
" messages to a value or promise in a future turn."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:741
msgid "0.1.9"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:743
msgid ""
"Added isRejected() for testing whether a value is a rejected promise.  "
"isResolved() retains the behavior of stating that rejected promises are "
"not resolved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:747
msgid "0.1.8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:749
msgid "Fixed isResolved(null) and isResolved(undefined) [issue #9]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:750
msgid "Fixed a problem with the Object.create shim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:752
msgid "0.1.7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:754
msgid ""
"shimmed ES5 Object.create in addition to Object.freeze for compatibility "
"on non-ES5 engines (gozala)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:757
msgid "0.1.6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:759
msgid "Q.isResolved added"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:760
msgid "promise.valueOf() now returns the value of resolved and near values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:762
msgid "asap retried"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:763
msgid "promises are frozen when possible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:765
msgid "0.1.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:767
msgid "fixed dependency list for Teleport (gozala)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:768
msgid "all unit tests now pass (gozala)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:770
msgid "0.1.4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/q_CHANGES.md:772
msgid "added support for Teleport as an engine (gozala)"
